{#- The plate catalogue: every illustration on the sub-site, once.

    Each plate is a Three.js scene from leynos/wireframe-3js, vendored at the
    pin in src/static/wireframe/assets/vendor/plates/PROVENANCE.txt by
    scripts/import_wireframe_plates.py, with the matching poster that stands
    in for it before the scene loads, under reduced motion, without WebGL,
    and in print. Titles are the source catalogue's. Words that must be read
    are here, in HTML, never only in the art.

    `alt` is the poster's description, the plate's one accessible
    representation; a civic setting that carries no technical claim is
    decorative and has an empty one. `kind` says what sort of picture it is
    (identity v0.4, section 11.1); `status` qualifies the claim it could be
    read as making, with `href` as its source when it has one. -#}
